Joyce, Samantha and Shannon -

I've created electronic payment campaigns to be linked to our Membership
and General Donation forms, allowing supporters to pay online if they wish
to donate when joining, or to make a general donation once or on a
recurring schedule.

Rather than duplicate all of the contact information on our website forms,
The campaign forms simply as ask folks to provide their full name (in
addition to payment info), so we can link their payment to the form they
completed on our website... a kind reminder that we need them to do both
forms... our website form and the Give Butter payment form.

I did not add a donation goal to the Membership campaign, but I did add a
$50,000 goal for the General Donation. Just a stab in the dark. I can
remove goal or change it. Thoughts?



Shannon -
If you log into our Give Butter site, you can see the 2 campaigns and the
links (both regular URL link and QR Code) that allow folks to move from the
online Membership or General Donation forms on our www.friendsofWDAC.org
website. We'll probably need a sentence or two to explain that folks need
to fill out the forms on our website, and then click on the Give Butter
link(s) to donate.

General Donation payment link -
https://givebutter.com/friends-of-the-wdac-general-donation
<https://givebutter.com/friends-of-the-wdac-general-donation>

Membership Donation payment link -
https://givebutter.com/become-a-friend-membership


All -
Please take a look at the published forms, and let me know if you have any
edits before we share with the wider community.


Thanks!

- Stephenie

